From 5ad5b78ccd14fa1191b16d6355f7617a8ba28d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SergiioB <sergiobarrientose@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:11:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xpu(qwen27): XPU_SPLIT runs part of each MLP on a second B70
 for decode rows

XPU_SPLIT=N puts N x 1,024 of the 17,408 MLP neurons of every layer on a peer
card. The peer holds only weight slices. The first card stores the MLP input
into the peer's memory and raises a flag word; the peer stores its part of the
down projection back. No peer atomics, no host round trip per exchange.
Prompt chunks stay on the first card. XPU_DEVICE picks the first card.

Screen on two Arc Pro B70 (PCIe 4.0 x8/x8), Qwen3.8-27B MLX 4-bit, 68-token
prompt, XPU_SPLIT=8: serial 33.1 -> 44.0 tok/s, drafted round 41.4 -> 35.7 ms,
drafted == serial. The text differs from the unsplit build (the two parts of
the down projection are rounded to fp16 before they are added).
